        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I've seen #1463, but I already have that behaviour for single windows. The problem lies w/ multiple windows at once.\r\n\r\nContent for not current (i.e. \"active\") windows is configured via `config.content.inactive` function. Use `%f` to make content show relative file path (see `:h 'statusline'`).\r\n\r\nSo something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.statusline').setup({\r\n  content = {\r\n    active = function()\r\n      -- Your content for active window\r\n    end,\r\n    inactive = function() return '%f' end,\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've seen <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"7788011\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1463\" data-hovercard-type=\"discussion\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1463/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1463\">#1463</a>, but I already have that behaviour for single windows. The problem lies w/ multiple windows at once.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Content for not current (i.e. \"active\") windows is configured via <code class=\"notranslate\">config.content.inactive</code> function. Use <code class=\"notranslate\">%f</code> to make content show relative file path (see <code class=\"notranslate\">:h 'statusline'</code>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require('mini.statusline').setup({\n  content = {\n    active = function()\n      -- Your content for active window\n    end,\n    inactive = function() return '%f' end,\n  },\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.statusline<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">content</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-en\">active</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n      <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Your content for active window</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n    <span class=\"pl-en\">inactive</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%f<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n  },\n})</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "I've seen #1463, but I already have that behaviour for single windows. The problem lies w/ multiple windows at once.\n\nContent for not current (i.e. \"active\") windows is configured via config.content.inactive function. Use %f to make content show relative file path (see :h 'statusline').\nSo something like this:\nrequire('mini.statusline').setup({\n  content = {\n    active = function()\n      -- Your content for active window\n    end,\n    inactive = function() return '%f' end,\n  },\n})",
